hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1578","We are told by Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’, we are told by Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray’, Sa’id told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Samurah bin Jundub and Imran bin Husayn remembered, and Samurah narrated that he had memorized two silences from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “One silence if He said “Allahu Akbar” and said “Allahu Akbar” when he finished reciting it when he bowed."
